  "result": "I implemented `slugify(text)` in `src/strings.js` and added 12 tests for it in `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes, 14 of 14 including the two existing `capitalize` tests.\n\nIt runs these steps in order:\n1. Lowercases the text.\n2. Turns `đ` into `d`.\n3. Strips diacritics.\n4. Turns each run of characters outside a-z and 0-9 into one hyphen.\n5. Trims leading hyphens.\n6. Cuts the result to 50 characters.\n7. Trims trailing hyphens, so a slug cut at 50 never ends in one.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- basic lowercasing and hyphenation\n- hyphen collapsing and trimming\n- Vietnamese text, `đ`/`Đ`, other Latin accents, and decomposed input\n- digits\n- empty and symbol-only input\n- the 50-character limit: a long slug is cut to 50, an exactly-50 slug is unchanged, and a cut never leaves a trailing hyphen\n\nI didn't commit anything.",
